## FABLE-006 — the two layout bugs

**The highlight frame now hugs the card.** It was placed at
`target.GetGlobalRect()`, and `GetGlobalRect()` ignores rotation. Hand cards sit
on a fan — up to about 10° each — so the gold frame was both the wrong shape and
visibly offset from the card it was pointing at. It now takes the target's full
global transform, so it is a true outline at any angle. (The same blindness to
rotation is why the lane frames never quite fit before FABLE-004 squared the
board.) Frames are plain `Panel`s now rather than `PanelContainer`s — they have
no children and are positioned by hand, so a container's layout pass could only
fight them.

**The victory panel stops overlapping itself.** Two causes, both in the same
family:

1. The Rewards block was a plain `Panel` wrapping a `VBoxContainer`. A `Panel` is
   not a container — it does not measure its children — so the entire rewards
   block reported **zero height**, and the buttons were laid out straight after
   the divider, on top of it. That is why "Turns taken" and "Shards" were behind
   `Fight Again`. It is a `PanelContainer` now. The outer panel already had a
   comment recording this exact lesson; the inner one was missed.
2. An autowrap `Label` reports a **one-line** minimum height, because it is
   entitled to wrap to whatever width it is given. The headline wraps to two
   lines and the outro flavour to three, so the panel asked for roughly 95px less
   than it draws and `panelVBox` squeezed everything below them. The wrapped
   labels now get their real measured height pinned, via the same `UiText`
   measurement added in FABLE-003.

